            "created_at": "2025-09-29T00:22:04.612308+00:00",
            "notes": "This is pretty much the same deal as round 6. We just get the weapon items that give the most weapon power, since we have what we need in other departments from our items/powers from earlier rounds. \n\nThe 100 armor from [Vital-E-Tee](item_b92e6f1d-3aac-4eec-b027-00c8e1529016) would still be good here, but it might be worth swapping it for another survival item or damage item. I haven't solved round 7 to be honest, since most of my games do not reach here. Maybe [Vanadium Injection](item_57953fbc-11ff-4e92-9928-fc59b7be668f) is good, but pulse still does 350 base damage, so its not bad.\n\n[Overdrive Core](item_a2a8dba1-5f2f-4da1-9445-b08f49162121) could also be really good since if your [Auto Recall](item_ae3dbebf-c306-4408-b698-6f666ace0a7c) pops, you  still have another life essentially.\n\nI also think its good to replace [Pulse Detector](item_79ddef46-8917-4d8f-a123-7ddb589ad3e7) for [The Closer](item_173c6d0f-dbe6-440e-924f-0ce08189ddce), since you just need 1 pellet of headshot to reveal an enemy for 3 seconds, which is really powerful.\n\nAs for powers, you realistically aren't getting enough crits in practice to make [Blink of an Eye](item_c1f6466f-b2ac-4b6a-ba48-b1531dfd686f) worth it, so the auto-aim from [Foresight](item_f4163ce1-8f80-43ca-85d4-39812084400f) actually feels so much better. \n\nThe other powers I don't think are as consistent or mesh well with the build, and I explain my reasoning in depth in the ***Round 5 Notes***.",
